    "result_text": "Done. The full suite (the single `AcceptanceTest` class, including the new `coreFormatsTelephoneDisplay` test) is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded a `telephoneDisplay` field: the stored E.164 telephone formatted for humans (`+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`), while `telephone` stays raw E.164.\n\nKept structural impact minimal by deriving the value in the existing MapStruct mapper rather than editing any of the three responder functions:\n\n- **`TelephoneDisplay.java`** (new) \u2014 a small, self-contained helper mirroring the existing `ContactPreference`/`Locality`/`AgeBand` pattern. Splits the country code (`+61` \u2192 2 digits, otherwise 1, matching `E164Telephone`) from the national digits and groups the latter in threes. Zero surrounding-class complexity to hold.\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one added `@Mapping` expression line, alongside the existing `ageBand`/`checkDigit` derivations, so every responder (get, created, updated) gets the field uniformly with no changes to their `service` methods.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared `telephoneDisplay` as a read-only string in the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the getter/setter.\n\nNo existing function was grown, and no large class was touched.",
